</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Results under different distributions</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we present similar results acquired with datasets collected from other sampling policies (random policy and half-expert policy).
The results under the half-expert dataset and the random dataset are shown in Table <a href="#A2.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Appendix B Results under different distributions ‣ How well can LLMs provide planning feedback in grounded environments?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> and Table <a href="#A2.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix B Results under different distributions ‣ How well can LLMs provide planning feedback in grounded environments?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, and show similar trends to results under the expert dataset.
We also observe random dataset results seem to have a larger variance since the dataset’s state distribution often only covers a small part of the state space.
For example, in Cliff Walking, a random policy has 75% of the chance to take any of the actions <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RIGHT</span>, <span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LEFT</span> or <span id="A2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DOWN</span> which results in hitting the wall or falling off the cliff.
Consequently, under the random policy, the agent almost never reaches the goal and mostly wanders around its start point.
The image observation results on VLMs under the half-expert dataset and the random dataset are shown in Table <a href="#A2.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix B Results under different distributions ‣ How well can LLMs provide planning feedback in grounded environments?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and Table <a href="#A2.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Appendix B Results under different distributions ‣ How well can LLMs provide planning feedback in grounded environments?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. The results, similar to LLM feedback, are consistent with results in the expert dataset, while the random dataset poses more challenges, as it contains unusual states. For example, the action advising accuracy for Qwen 2.5 VL 72B dropped to 8%.</p>
</div>
