</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="823.11" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 823.11" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,823.11) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 817.21 C 0 820.47 2.64 823.11 5.91 823.11 L 544.09 823.11 C 547.36 823.11 550 820.47 550 817.21 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 801.69 L 548.03 801.69 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 807.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Delta Action in Robomimic</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:55.9em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="776.11" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 773.42)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are a robot engineer. You need to control a robot arm to lift an object. You need to observe the robot’s current state and choose which action to do next in order to lift the object. You can move the robot in the X, Y, or Z direction, as well as open/close its gripper. The robot’s state is given in the following format:</span></span><pre id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
    Gripper position: [x y z ]
    Object position: [x y z]
    Object relative distance to gripper: [dx dy dz]
    Gripper finger state: open or closed
</pre>
<span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You can choose actions that move the gripper in the X, Y, Z direction, with additional control of the gripper. The format of the action is:</span></span><pre id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
[resulting x, resulting y, resulting z, ignore, ignore, ignore, resulting gripper state]
</pre>
<span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Note on the gripper: Set grip to 1 to open the gripper and -1 to close the gripper. The robot’s gripper should be closed if it is beginning to grasp the object, or when it is holding the object. When it is approaching the object, the gripper is open. If the robot gripper needs to be closed, you should continue to close the gripper, even if it is closed. Similarly, if the robot gripper needs to be open, you should continue to open the gripper, even if it is already open.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You current observation is:</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Gripper position: [-0.01261643 0.02076922 0.82920151]

<br class="ltx_break">Object position: [-0.02050141 0.02279622 0.82019789]

<br class="ltx_break">Object relative position to gripper: [ 0.00788497 -0.002027 0.00900362]

<br class="ltx_break">Gripper finger position: [ 0.03368153 -0.03366622]

<br class="ltx_break">Gripper status: +1</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Given the following actions, which action is better? Please think step by step.</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Index 0: [ 0.25368214 0.02193805 -0.23200776 0.00478249 0.25400147 0.01591277 1. ]

<br class="ltx_break">Index 1: [-0.30631787 0.02193805 -0.23200776 0.00478249 0.25400147 0.01591277 1. ]

<br class="ltx_break">Index 2: [-0.02631785 0.30193806 -0.23200776 0.00478249 0.25400147 0.01591277 1. ]

<br class="ltx_break">Index 3: [-0.02631785 -0.25806195 -0.23200776 0.00478249 0.25400147 0.01591277 1. ]

<br class="ltx_break">Index 4: [-0.02631785 0.02193805 0.04799224 0.00478249 0.25400147 0.01591277 1. ]

<br class="ltx_break">Index 5: [-0.02631785 0.02193805 -0.5120078 0.00478249 0.25400147 0.01591277 1. ]

<br class="ltx_break">Index 12: [-0.02631785 0.02193805 -0.23200776 0.00478249 0.25400147 0.01591277 1. ]

<br class="ltx_break">Index 13: [-0.02631785 0.02193805 -0.23200776 0.00478249 0.25400147 0.01591277 -1. ]</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You should consider the position of the robot gripper and object, and how they are related to each other. For example, if the robot gripper is on the left of the object, you should consider moving the robot gripper to the right.
<br class="ltx_break">Only give the answer in a new line in JSON format:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": &lt;REASONING&gt;, "index": &lt;INDEX&gt;}
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Where <span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.10.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;INDEX&gt;</span> is one of action choice index, <span id="A5.SS1.p5.pic1.2.10.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;REASONING&gt;</span> is a string of your thinking steps.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="328.44" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 328.44" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,328.44) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 322.53 C 0 325.8 2.64 328.44 5.91 328.44 L 544.09 328.44 C 547.36 328.44 550 325.8 550 322.53 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 304.33 L 548.03 304.33 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 312.93)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Goal Advising in Cliff Walking</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:19.95em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="278.74" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 276.05)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are an agent trying to move to position (3, 11).
<br class="ltx_break">You can take 4 possible actions:</span></span><pre id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
  - going UP
  - going DOWN
  - going LEFT
  - going RIGHT
</pre>
<span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The grid world is 4x12 with zero-indexed positions. There are holes on the grid that you do not know. Do not exceed the boundaries of the world, and do not fall into the holes. You will be asked to predict the best next state given a state.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are in position (3, 0). What coordinates should you move to in the next step? Please think step by step.
<br class="ltx_break">Only give the answer in a new line in JSON format:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": &lt;REASONING&gt;, "row": &lt;ROW&gt;, "column": &lt;COLUMN&gt;}
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Where <span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.2.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;ROW&gt;</span> is the number of the row you should move, and <span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.2.4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;COLUMN&gt;</span> is the number of column you should move, <span id="A5.SS1.p6.pic1.2.4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;REASONING&gt;</span> is a string of your thinking steps.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>In Context Learning Prompt Examples</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide prompt examples for our ICL experiments. We insert these examples after the description of the task, right before providing the current observation and querying for feedback.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1768.72" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 1768.72" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1768.72) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 1762.81 C 0 1766.07 2.64 1768.72 5.91 1768.72 L 544.09 1768.72 C 547.36 1768.72 550 1766.07 550 1762.81 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 1744.61 L 548.03 1744.61 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 1753.2)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Cliff Walking Goal Advising ICL Example</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 1196.15)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:38.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:85.45em;font-size:10pt;" height="1719.04" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 536.65)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Below are examples about reasoning over the best next state.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> You are in position (3, 0). What coordinates should you move to in the next step?
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Answer:<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": "There are 4 neighbouring coordinates: (2, 0), (4, 0), (3, -1), (3, 1). If I move to (2, 0), it is a safe place. If I move to (4, 0), I will hit the wall as I am in a zero-indexed 4x12 grid and (4, 0) is outside of boundary. If I move to (3, -1), I will similarly hit the wall as (3, -1) is outside of boundary. If I move to (3, 1) and since there are holes in (3, 1) ... (3, 10), I will fall into a hole. Therefore moving to (2, 0) is the only safe option.","row": "2", "column": "0"}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> You are in position (2, 11). What coordinates should you move to in the next step?
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Answer:<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": "There are 4 neighbouring coordinates: (1, 11), (3, 11), (2, 10) and (2, 12). If I move to (1, 11) and then I will need 2 steps as (1, 11) -&gt; (2, 11) -&gt; (3, 11) to reach the goal (3, 11). If I move to (3, 11) I will reach the goal. If I move to (2, 10) and then I need 3 steps as (2, 10) -&gt; (3, 10) -&gt; (3, 11) to reach the goal. If I move to (2, 12) I will hit the wall as it is outside of boundary. Therefore (3, 11) is the best option.","row": "3", "column": "11"}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> You are in position (1, 5). What coordinates should you move to in the next step?
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Answer:<span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A5.SS2.p2.pic1.2.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": "There are 4 possible action: (0, 5), (2, 5), (1, 6), (1, 4). If I move to (0, 5) and I will need 9 steps to reach goal: (0, 5) -&gt; (0, 6) -&gt; (0, 7) -&gt; (0, 8) -&gt; (0, 9) -&gt; (0, 10) -&gt; (0, 11) -&gt; (1, 11) -&gt; (2, 11) -&gt; (3, 11). If I move to (2, 5) and I will need 7 steps to reach goal: (2, 5) -&gt; (2, 6) -&gt; (2, 7) -&gt; (2, 8) -&gt; (2, 9) -&gt; (2, 10) -&gt; (2, 11) -&gt; (3, 11). If I move to (1, 6) and I will need 7 steps to reach goal: (1, 6) -&gt; (1, 7) -&gt; (1, 8) -&gt; (1, 9) -&gt; (1, 10) -&gt; (1, 11) -&gt; (2, 11) -&gt; (3, 11). If I move to (1, 4) and I will need 9 steps to reach goal: (1, 4) -&gt; (1, 5) -&gt; (1, 6) -&gt; (1, 7) -&gt; (1, 8) -&gt; (1, 9) -&gt; (1, 10) -&gt; (1, 11) -&gt; (2, 11) -&gt; (3, 11). Therefore, (1, 6) and (2, 5) are the best next coordinates as they give shortest path to goal. I just need one good coordinates so I will pick one from (1, 6) and (2, 5)","row": "2", "column": "5"}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="689.32" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 689.32" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,689.32) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 683.41 C 0 686.67 2.64 689.32 5.91 689.32 L 544.09 689.32 C 547.36 689.32 550 686.67 550 683.41 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 665.21 L 548.03 665.21 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 673.8)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Door Key Binary Feedback ICL</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 67.05)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:42.38em;--ltx-fo-depth:3.85em;font-size:10pt;" height="639.62" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 586.35)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer:<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": "The agent is facing a wall, so moving forward does nothing and fails to progress toward picking up the key. A turn to face the key is a better action.", "feedback": "NO"}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> You are in the following state represented in ascii art:</span></span></span><pre id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
#####
#.D.#
#ˆ#.#
#.#G#
#####
</pre>
<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The door is locked. You have the key.
<br class="ltx_break">Is action MOVE FORWARD the best action you can take? Please think step by step.
<br class="ltx_break">Only give the answer in a new line in JSON format:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": &lt;REASONING&gt;, "feedback": &lt;FEEDBACK&gt;}
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Where <span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;FEEDBACK&gt;</span> is one of “YES” or “NO”, <span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;REASONING&gt;</span> is a string of your thinking steps.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer:<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": "You already have the key, so the immediate goal is to move adjacent to the locked door and unlock it. The tile directly ahead is free, and moving forward places you in position to turn and unlock the door. Therefore, moving forward is the best action.", "feedback": "YES"}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> You are in the following state represented in ascii art:</span></span></span><pre id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
#####
#.#.#
#.&gt;.#
#.#G#
#####
</pre>
<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The door is unlocked. You have the key.
<br class="ltx_break">Is action TURN LEFT the best action you can take? Please think step by step.
<br class="ltx_break">Only give the answer in a new line in JSON format:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": &lt;REASONING&gt;, "feedback": &lt;FEEDBACK&gt;}
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Where <span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.8.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;FEEDBACK&gt;</span> is one of “YES” or “NO”, <span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.8.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;REASONING&gt;</span> is a string of your thinking steps.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer:<span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A5.SS2.p3.pic1.2.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": "The agent is facing right and needs to move toward the goal on its right and then turn down. Turning left would make the agent face upwards into a wall. Moving forward is the better move.", "feedback": "NO"}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="394.86" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 394.86" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,394.86) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 388.95 C 0 392.21 2.64 394.86 5.91 394.86 L 544.09 394.86 C 547.36 394.86 550 392.21 550 388.95 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 370.75 L 548.03 370.75 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 379.34)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Action Advising ICL Four Rooms</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 50.45)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:22.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:2.65em;font-size:10pt;" height="345.16" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 308.49)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Below are examples about reasoning over the best action.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">You are in the following state represented in ascii art:
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span><pre id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
###################
#........#........#
#........#........#
#........#........#
#........#........#
#........#........#
#........#........#
#........#........#
#.................#
######.##########.#
#........#....G.&lt;.#
#........#........#
#........#........#
#.................#
#........#........#
#........#........#
#........#........#
#........#........#
###################
</pre>
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Which action do you choose? Please think step by step.
<br class="ltx_break">Only give the answer in a new line in JSON format:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": &lt;REASONING&gt;, "action": &lt;ACTION&gt;}
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Where <span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;ACTION&gt;</span> is one of “TURN LEFT”, “TURN RIGHT” or “MOVE FORWARD”, <span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;REASONING&gt;</span> is a string of your thinking steps.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer:<span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A5.SS2.p4.pic1.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": "The agent is already facing left and the goal is two tiles to its left, so moving forward brings it closer to the goal.", "action": "MOVE FORWARD"}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS2.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="834.03" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 834.03" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,834.03) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 828.12 C 0 831.38 2.64 834.03 5.91 834.03 L 544.09 834.03 C 547.36 834.03 550 831.38 550 828.12 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 809.92 L 548.03 809.92 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 818.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
