<span id="A5.I3.i11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I3.i11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">move to meadow from forest</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.SS2.p5.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Given <span id="A5.SS2.p5.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">craft crafting table</span> or <span id="A5.SS2.p5.pic1.2.5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">craft wood pickaxe</span>, which action is better? Please think step by step.
<br class="ltx_break">Only give the answer in a new line in JSON format:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.pic1.2.5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": &lt;REASONING&gt;, "preference": &lt;PREFERENCE&gt;}
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Where <span id="A5.SS2.p5.pic1.2.5.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PREFERENCE&gt;</span> is one of “FIRST” or “SECOND”, <span id="A5.SS2.p5.pic1.2.5.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;REASONING&gt;</span> is a string of your thinking steps.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS2.p5.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer:<span id="A5.SS2.p5.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A5.SS2.p5.pic1.2.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": "We already have access to a crafting table in the forest, so crafting another is not immediately useful. We need a wood pickaxe to gather stone and progress toward diamonds.", "preference": "SECOND"}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1059.03" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 1059.03" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1059.03) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 1053.13 C 0 1056.39 2.64 1059.03 5.91 1059.03 L 544.09 1059.03 C 547.36 1059.03 550 1056.39 550 1053.13 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 1034.92 L 548.03 1034.92 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 1043.52)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">ALF World ICL Binary Feedback Example</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 83.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:67.9em;--ltx-fo-depth:5.05em;font-size:10pt;" height="1009.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 939.47)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">You received instruction: Place a chilled tomato in a microwave.
<br class="ltx_break">Your observation is: You arrive at loc 3. On the shelf 2, you see a creditcard 2.
<br class="ltx_break">Your inventory: tomato 1.
Below is your history:</span></span></span><pre id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
You received instruction: Place a chilled tomato in a microwave.
Your observation is: You are in the middle of a room. Looking quickly around
you, you see a cabinet 6, a cabinet 5, a cabinet 4, a cabinet 3, a cabinet 2,
a cabinet 1, a coffeemachine 1, a countertop 3, a countertop 2, a countertop 1,
a drawer 3, a drawer 2, a drawer 1, a fridge 1, a garbagecan 1, a microwave 1,
a shelf 3, a shelf 2, a shelf 1, a sinkbasin 1, a stoveburner 4, a stoveburner 3,
a stoveburner 2, a stoveburner 1, and a toaster 1.
Your inventory: empty.
You took action: go to cabinet 1.

You received instruction: Place a chilled tomato in a microwave.
Your observation is: You arrive at loc 13. On the cabinet 1, you see a bowl 1.
Your inventory: empty.
You took action: go to countertop 1.

&lt;More History Steps Ommited for Ease of Reading&gt;
</pre>
<span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You can take the following actions:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">examine shelf 2
<br class="ltx_break">examine tomato 1
<br class="ltx_break">go to cabinet 1
<br class="ltx_break">go to cabinet 2
<br class="ltx_break">go to cabinet 3
<br class="ltx_break">go to cabinet 4
<br class="ltx_break">go to cabinet 5
<br class="ltx_break">go to cabinet 6
<br class="ltx_break">go to coffeemachine 1
<br class="ltx_break">go to countertop 1
<br class="ltx_break">go to countertop 2
<br class="ltx_break">go to countertop 3
<br class="ltx_break">go to drawer 1
<br class="ltx_break">go to drawer 2
<br class="ltx_break">go to drawer 3
<br class="ltx_break">go to fridge 1
<br class="ltx_break">go to garbagecan 1
<br class="ltx_break">go to microwave 1
<br class="ltx_break">go to shelf 1
<br class="ltx_break">go to shelf 3
<br class="ltx_break">go to sinkbasin 1
<br class="ltx_break">go to stoveburner 1
<br class="ltx_break">go to stoveburner 2
<br class="ltx_break">go to stoveburner 3
<br class="ltx_break">go to stoveburner 4
<br class="ltx_break">go to toaster 1
<br class="ltx_break">inventory
<br class="ltx_break">look
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Is action <span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">go to cabinet 3</span> the best action you can take? Please think step by step.
<br class="ltx_break">Only give the answer in a new line in JSON format:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": &lt;REASONING&gt;, "feedback": &lt;FEEDBACK&gt;}
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Where <span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;FEEDBACK&gt;</span> is one of “YES” or “NO”, <span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;REASONING&gt;</span> is a string of your thinking steps.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer:<span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A5.SS2.p6.pic1.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": "We already have the chilled tomato in our inventory and our goal is to place it in the microwave. The next logical step is to go back to the microwave and open it, then put the tomato inside. Going to cabinet 3 does not help achieve this goal.", "feedback": "NO"}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Thinking Guides Prompt Examples</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we show the example prompts of thinking guides. We insert these thinking guides inside standard prompts, right after we describe the domain and before we provide the current observation and query for feedback.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS3.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="178.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 178.23" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,178.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 172.33 C 0 175.59 2.64 178.23 5.91 178.23 L 544.09 178.23 C 547.36 178.23 550 175.59 550 172.33 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 154.12 L 548.03 154.12 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 162.72)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS3.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Thinking Guides for Door Key and Four Rooms</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:9.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="128.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 125.84)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS3.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS3.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You should think about these questions.
<br class="ltx_break">What is your current goal?
<br class="ltx_break">Based on the rules you know, what subgoals do you need to achieve?
<br class="ltx_break">Based on what you see and what you have, what subgoals have you achieved?
<br class="ltx_break">If you have not achieved all of the subgoals, based on the rules and doable actions, can you achieve any subgoals now?
<br class="ltx_break">If yes, which subgoal do you want to achieve next?
<br class="ltx_break">If no, what do you need or where should you go next?</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS3.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="178.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 178.23" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,178.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 172.33 C 0 175.59 2.64 178.23 5.91 178.23 L 544.09 178.23 C 547.36 178.23 550 175.59 550 172.33 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 154.12 L 548.03 154.12 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 162.72)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS3.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS3.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Thinking Guides for HierachyCraft</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:9.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="128.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 125.84)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS3.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS3.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You should think about these questions. 
<br class="ltx_break">You need to get a diamond. 
<br class="ltx_break">Based on the rules you know, what subgoals do you need to achieve? 
<br class="ltx_break">Based on what you see and what you have, what subgoals have you achieved? 
<br class="ltx_break">If you have not achieved all of the subgoals, based on the rules and doable actions, can you achieve any subgoals now? 
<br class="ltx_break">If yes, which subgoal do you want to achieve next? 
<br class="ltx_break">If no, what do you need or where should you go next?</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS3.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="161.63" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 161.63" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,161.63) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 155.72 C 0 158.98 2.64 161.63 5.91 161.63 L 544.09 161.63 C 547.36 161.63 550 158.98 550 155.72 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 137.52 L 548.03 137.52 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 146.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS3.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS3.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Thinking Guides for Cliff Walking</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:7.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="111.93" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 109.24)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS3.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS3.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You should think about these questions. 
<br class="ltx_break">What is your current goal? 
<br class="ltx_break">Based on the rules you know, which coordinates do you need to reach the goal? 
<br class="ltx_break">Based on what you see and what you known, can you reach any of the coordinates now? 
<br class="ltx_break">If no, comparing the possible actions you can take, which one leads you closer to the goal?</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS3.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="178.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 178.23" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,178.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 172.33 C 0 175.59 2.64 178.23 5.91 178.23 L 544.09 178.23 C 547.36 178.23 550 175.59 550 172.33 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 154.12 L 548.03 154.12 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 162.72)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS3.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS3.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Thinking Guides for ALF World</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:9.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="128.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 125.84)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS3.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS3.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You should think about these questions. 
<br class="ltx_break">What is your current goal? 
<br class="ltx_break">Based on the rules you know, what subgoals do you need to achieve? 
<br class="ltx_break">Based on what you see and what you have, what subgoals have you achieved? 
<br class="ltx_break">If you have not achieved all of the subgoals, based on the rules and doable actions, can you achieve any subgoals now? 
<br class="ltx_break">If yes, which subgoal do you want to achieve next? 
<br class="ltx_break">If no, what do you need or where should you go next? 
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Dynamics Hint Prompt Examples</h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we show prompt examples of experiments with/without dynamics hints. For unknown dynamics, we alter the task description at the beginning of the prompt and remove anything related to dynamics.
For fully known dynamics, we append the rules of the game right after we describe the task before we provide states and query for feedback.
For history context, we append the history steps at the end of the prompt, right after we provide the current observation and query for feedback.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS4.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="126.5" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 126.5" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,126.5) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 120.59 C 0 123.85 2.64 126.5 5.91 126.5 L 544.09 126.5 C 547.36 126.5 550 123.85 550 120.59 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 102.39 L 548.03 102.39 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 110.98)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS4.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Cliff Walking Unknown Dynamics</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:5.55em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="76.8" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 76.8)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS4.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS4.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are an agent trying to move to position (3, 11). 
<br class="ltx_break">You can take 4 possible actions:</span></span><pre id="A5.SS4.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
- going UP
- going DOWN
- going LEFT
- going RIGHT
</pre>
<span id="A5.SS4.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The grid world is 4x12 with zero-indexed positions. There are holes on the grid that you do not know. Do not exceed the boundaries of the world, and do not fall into the holes.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS4.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="162.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 162.4" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,162.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 156.49 C 0 159.75 2.64 162.4 5.91 162.4 L 544.09 162.4 C 547.36 162.4 550 159.75 550 156.49 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 138.29 L 548.03 138.29 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 146.88)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS4.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS4.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Cliff Walking History Context Example</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:7.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="112.7" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 109.24)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS4.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS4.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Here is the history of your actions:</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS4.p3.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p3.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 1: You were at position (3, 0), and you took action UP, then you reached (2, 0).</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS4.p3.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p3.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 2: You were at position (2, 0), and you took action DOWN, then you reached (3, 0).</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS4.p3.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p3.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 3: You were at position (3, 0), and you took action RIGHT, then you reached (3, 0). You fell into the holes.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS4.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="241.96" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 241.96" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,241.96) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 236.05 C 0 239.31 2.64 241.96 5.91 241.96 L 544.09 241.96 C 547.36 241.96 550 239.31 550 236.05 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 217.85 L 548.03 217.85 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 226.44)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS4.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS4.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Door Key Unknown Dynamics Example</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:13.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="192.26" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 192.26)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS4.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS4.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You need to solve Minigrid Doorkey.
Minigrid Doorkey involves crossing a gridworld, where you need to pick up the key, unlock the door and reach the goal. Do not hit the wall.
The state is described with an ASCII art. In the ASCII art, “#” means wall. “K” means key. “D” means door. “G” means goal. “.” means empty tile. “ˆ” means the agent who is facing upwards. “V” means the agent who is facing downwards. “&lt;” means the agent who is facing leftwards. “&gt;” means the agent who is facing rightwards.
The possible actions are:</span></span><pre id="A5.SS4.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
    1. TURN LEFT
    2. TURN RIGHT
    3. MOVE FORWARD
    4. PICK UP THE KEY
    5. UNLOCK THE DOOR
</pre>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="324.98" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 324.98" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,324.98) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 319.07 C 0 322.34 2.64 324.98 5.91 324.98 L 544.09 324.98 C 547.36 324.98 550 322.34 550 319.07 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 300.87 L 548.03 300.87 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 309.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Door Key History Context Example</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:19.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="275.28" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 275.28)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Here is the history of your actions:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1:</span> You see:</span></span><pre id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
#####
#K#.#
#.D.#
#&lt;#G#
#####
</pre>
<span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You don’t have the key and the door is locked. You took action <span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TURN RIGHT</span>.
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2:</span> You see:</span></span><pre id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
#####
#K#.#
#.D.#
#ˆ#G#
#####
</pre>
<span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You don’t have the key and the door is locked. You took action <span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MOVE FORWARD</span>.
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3:</span> You see:</span></span><pre id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
#####
#K#.#
#ˆD.#
#.#G#
#####
</pre>
<span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You don’t have the key. The door is locked. You took action <span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PICK UP THE KEY</span>.
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4:</span> You see:</span></span><pre id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
#####
#.#.#
#ˆD.#
#.#G#
#####
</pre>
<span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You have the key. The door is locked. You took action <span id="A5.SS4.p5.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TURN RIGHT</span>.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS4.p6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="624.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 624.4" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,624.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 618.5 C 0 621.76 2.64 624.4 5.91 624.4 L 544.09 624.4 C 547.36 624.4 550 621.76 550 618.5 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 600.29 L 548.03 600.29 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 608.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS4.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS4.p6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">HierachyCraft Full Dynamics Example</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 14.32)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:34.88em;--ltx-fo-height:41.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.04em;font-size:10pt;" height="574.71" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 574.17)" width="482.64"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS4.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:34.88em;">
<span id="A5.SS4.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Below are the rules for the minecraft.</span></span><pre id="A5.SS4.p6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
You need a crafting table to craft something.
You need a furnace to smelt something.
You can pick up a crafting table or a furnace and take them around.
You need to place one in your current area if you want to use them.
You can get 3 iron ingot after smelting with 3 iron ore, 2 wood plank.
You can get 3 gold ingot after smelting with 3 gold ore, 2 wood plank.
You can get 8 iron ingot after smelting with 8 iron ore, 1 coal.
You can get 8 gold ingot after smelting with 8 gold ore, 1 coal.
You can craft 4 wood plank with 1 wood.
You can craft 4 stick with 2 wood plank.
You can craft 1 furnace with 8 cobblestone.
You can craft 3 paper with 3 reeds.
You can craft 1 book with 3 paper, 1 leather.
You can craft 1 enchanting table with 1 book, 4 obsidian, 2 diamond.
You can craft 1 clock with 4 gold ingot, 1 redstone.
You can craft 1 flint with 10 gravel.
You can craft 4 flint and steel with 1 iron ingot, 1 flint.
You can craft 2 blaze powder with 1 blaze rod.
You can craft 1 ender eye with 1 blaze powder, 1 ender pearl.
You can craft 10 wood pickaxe with 3 wood plank, 2 stick.
You can craft 10 wood axe with 3 wood plank, 2 stick.
You can craft 10 wood shovel with 1 wood plank, 2 stick.
You can craft 10 wood sword with 2 wood plank, 1 stick.
You can craft 20 stone pickaxe with 3 cobblestone, 2 stick.
You can craft 20 stone axe with 3 cobblestone, 2 stick.
You can craft 20 stone shovel with 1 cobblestone, 2 stick.
You can craft 20 stone sword with 2 cobblestone, 1 stick.
You can craft 40 iron pickaxe with 3 iron ingot, 2 stick.
You can craft 40 iron axe with 3 iron ingot, 2 stick.
You can craft 40 iron shovel with 1 iron ingot, 2 stick.
You can craft 40 iron sword with 2 iron ingot, 1 stick.
You can craft 10 gold pickaxe with 3 gold ingot, 2 stick.
You can craft 10 gold axe with 3 gold ingot, 2 stick.
You can craft 10 gold shovel with 1 gold ingot, 2 stick.
You can craft 10 gold sword with 2 gold ingot, 1 stick.
You can craft 100 diamond pickaxe with 3 diamond, 2 stick.
You can craft 100 diamond axe with 3 diamond, 2 stick.
You can craft 100 diamond shovel with 1 diamond, 2 stick.
You can craft 100 diamond sword with 2 diamond, 1 stick.
You can collect 2 dirt at forest.
You can collect 2 dirt at swamp.
You can collect 2 dirt at meadow.
You need to have at least 1 diamond shovel to collect 16 dirt at forest.
1 diamond shovel will be consumed.
&lt;The rest are omitted&gt;

</pre>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.5 </span>Egocentric Prompt Examples</h3>

<div id="A5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In MiniGrids Egocentric Observation experiments, the ASCII arts are rotated so that the agent is always facing forward.
In Robomimic experiments, we verbalise the observation with relative position to the object.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="534.76" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 534.76" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,534.76) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 528.86 C 0 532.12 2.64 534.76 5.91 534.76 L 544.09 534.76 C 547.36 534.76 550 532.12 550 528.86 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 510.65 L 548.03 510.65 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 519.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Door Key with Egocentric Observation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:34.86em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="485.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 482.38)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You need to solve Minigrid Doorkey.
<br class="ltx_break">Minigrid Doorkey involves crossing a gridworld, where you need to pick up the key, unlock the door and reach the goal. Do not hit the wall.
<br class="ltx_break">The state is described with an ASCII art in first-person perspective. In the ASCII art, “#” means wall. “K” means key. “D” means door. “G” means goal. “.” means empty tile.
<br class="ltx_break">“ˆ” is where you are. You are always facing forward.
<br class="ltx_break">The possible actions are:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A5.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">TURN LEFT.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">TURN RIGHT.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">MOVE FORWARD, moving forwards for one tile</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">PICK UP THE KEY, picking up the key, this is only possible when you are facing the tile with key on it.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">UNLOCK THE DOOR, this action is only possible when you have the key.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You will be asked to predict the best action given a state.
<br class="ltx_break">You are in the following state represented in ASCII art:</span></span><pre id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
#####
#..G#
##D##
#.ˆ.#
#####
</pre>
<span id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The door is locked. You have the key.
<br class="ltx_break">Which action do you choose? Please think step by step.
<br class="ltx_break">Only give the answer in a new line in JSON format:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": &lt;REASONING&gt;, "action": &lt;ACTION&gt;}
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Where <span id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.2.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;ACTION&gt;</span> is one of “TURN LEFT”, “TURN RIGHT”, “MOVE FORWARD”, “PICK UP THE KEY” or “UNLOCK THE DOOR”, <span id="A5.SS5.p2.pic1.2.4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;REASONING&gt;</span> is a string of your thinking steps.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="898.45" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 898.45" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,898.45) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 892.54 C 0 895.8 2.64 898.45 5.91 898.45 L 544.09 898.45 C 547.36 898.45 550 895.8 550 892.54 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 874.34 L 548.03 874.34 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 882.93)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Door Key with Egocentric Observation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:61.15em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="848.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 846.07)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are a robot arm trying to lift an object. You can move your gripper in the X, Y, or Z direction, as well as open/close your gripper. Each step, you see:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A5.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Relative distance from your gripper to object in x direction</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Relative distance from your gripper to object in y direction</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Relative distance from your gripper in z direction</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Gripper finger state: open or closed</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You can choose actions that move the gripper in the X, Y, Z direction, with additional control of the gripper.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Note on the gripper:<span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> You should close it when beginning to grasp the object, or when you are holding the object. When you are approaching the object, the gripper should be open. If the gripper needs to be closed, you should continue to close the gripper, even if it is closed. Similarly, if the gripper needs to be open, you should continue to open the gripper, even if it is already open.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You current observation is:<span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A5.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The object is 0.002046926351863232 to the right of your gripper.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The object is 0.024008545831402408 in front of your gripper.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I6.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The object is 0.8217841891593334 below your gripper.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Given the following action:
[-0.2087612 -0.02484818 -0.16213629 0.01804361 -0.04799016 0.00671699 0.9998945 ]</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Here is a list of corrective actions that you can take. Each action will modify the current gripper state by the action amount. Which action do you choose? Please think step by step.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A5.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Action 0: Move gripper forward by 0.28</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Action 1: Move gripper backward by 0.28</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Action 2: Move gripper right by 0.28</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I7.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I7.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I7.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I7.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Action 3: Move gripper left by 0.28</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I7.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I7.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I7.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I7.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Action 4: Move gripper vertically upward by 0.28</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I7.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I7.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I7.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I7.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Action 5: Move gripper vertically downward by 0.28</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I7.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I7.i7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.I7.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I7.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Action 6: Open gripper</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I7.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I7.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I7.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I7.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Action 7: Close gripper</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You should consider the position of the robot gripper and object, and how they are related to each other. For example, if the robot gripper is on the left of the object, you should consider moving the robot gripper to the right.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Only give the answer in a new line in JSON format:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": &lt;REASONING&gt;, "index": &lt;INDEX&gt;}
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Where <span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.8.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;INDEX&gt;</span> is one of action choice index, <span id="A5.SS5.p3.pic1.2.8.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;REASONING&gt;</span> is a string of your thinking steps.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.6 </span>VLM Feedback Prompt Examples</h3>

<div id="A5.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="710" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 710" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,710) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 704.09 C 0 707.35 2.64 710 5.91 710 L 544.09 710 C 547.36 710 550 707.35 550 704.09 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 685.89 L 548.03 685.89 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 694.48)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Door Key with Image Observation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:47.72em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="660.31" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 660.31)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You need to solve Minigrid Doorkey. Minigrid Doorkey involves crossing a gridworld, where you need to pick up the key, unlock the door and reach the goal. Do not hit the wall. The state is depicted in an image.</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is you facing upwards. <img src="2509.09790v1/pics/doorkey/UP.png" id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:21/21;" width="21" height="21" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is you facing right. <img src="2509.09790v1/pics/doorkey/RIGHT.png" id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:21/21;" width="21" height="21" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is you facing down. <img src="2509.09790v1/pics/doorkey/DOWN.png" id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:21/21;" width="21" height="21" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is you facing left. <img src="2509.09790v1/pics/doorkey/LEFT.png" id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:21/21;" width="21" height="21" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is an empty tile. <img src="2509.09790v1/pics/doorkey/EMPTY.png" id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:21/21;" width="21" height="21" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is a key. <img src="2509.09790v1/pics/doorkey/KEY.png" id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.g6" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:21/21;" width="21" height="21" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is a locked door. <img src="2509.09790v1/pics/doorkey/DOOR_LOCKED.png" id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.g7" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:21/21;" width="21" height="21" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is an unlocked door. <img src="2509.09790v1/pics/doorkey/DOOR_UNLOCKED.png" id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.g8" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:21/21;" width="21" height="21" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is your goal. <img src="2509.09790v1/pics/doorkey/GOAL.png" id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.g9" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:21/21;" width="21" height="21" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is a wall. <img src="2509.09790v1/pics/doorkey/WALL.png" id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.g10" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:21/21;" width="21" height="21" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
The possible actions are: 1. TURN LEFT, changing the direction to left 2. TURN RIGHT, changing the direction to right 3. MOVE FORWARD, moving forwards for one tile 4. PICK UP THE KEY, picking up the key, this is only possible when you are facing the tile with key on it 5. UNLOCK THE DOOR, this action is only possible when you have the key. Is action TURN LEFT the best action you can take? Please think step by step. Only give the answer in a new line in JSON format: <span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": &lt;REASONING&gt;,"feedback": &lt;FEEDBACK&gt;}
<br class="ltx_break"></span>where &lt;FEEDBACK&gt; is one of "YES" or "NO", &lt;REASONING&gt; is a string of your thinking steps.</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is your image observation.</span></span><img src="2509.09790v1/pics/doorkey/obs.png" id="A5.SS6.p1.pic1.g11" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:202/202;" width="202" height="202" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="A5.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="733" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 733" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,733) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 727.09 C 0 730.35 2.64 733 5.91 733 L 544.09 733 C 547.36 733 550 730.35 550 727.09 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 708.89 L 548.03 708.89 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 717.48)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Robomimic with Image Observation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:49.19em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="683.31" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 680.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are a robot engineer. You need to control a robot arm to lift an object. You need to observe the robot’s current state and choose which action to do next in order to lift the object. You can move the robot in the X, Y, or Z direction, as well as open/close its gripper. You will also recieve a image as your observation. You can choose actions that move the gripper in the X, Y, Z direction, with additional control of the gripper. The format of the action is:
<br class="ltx_break">n [ resulting x, resulting y, resulting z, ignore, ignore, ignore, resulting gripper state]
<br class="ltx_break">nIn the image, you will see you are facing the robot and a red cube (the object) is on the table. When dx &lt; 0, the gripper moves away from you. When dx &gt; 0, the gripper moves towards you. When dy &lt; 0, the gripper moves towards the left of the picture. When dy &gt; 0, the gripper moves towards the right of the picture. When dz &lt; 0, the gripper moves towards the table. When dz &gt; 0, the gripper moves away from the table.
<br class="ltx_break">n Note on the gripper: Set grip to 1 to open the gripper and -1 to close the gripper. The robot’s gripper should be closed if it is beginning to grasp the object, or when it is holding the object. When it is approaching the object, the gripper is open. If the robot gripper needs to be closed, you should continue to close the gripper, even if it is closed. Similarly, if the robot gripper needs to be open, you should continue to open the gripper, even if it is already open.</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Your image observation is:</span></span><img src="2509.09790v1/pics/robomimic/obs.png" id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:202/202;" width="202" height="202" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
<span id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Which action do you choose? Please think step by step. You should consider the position of the robot gripper and object, and how they are related to each other. For example, if the robot gripper is on the left of the object, you should consider moving the robot gripper to the right. Only give the answer in a new line in JSON format:</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{"reasoning": &lt;REASONING&gt;, "action": &lt;ACTION&gt;}<span id="A5.SS6.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
where &lt;ACTION&gt; is the optimal action following the format of (dx, dy, dz), &lt;REASONING&gt; is a string of your thinking steps.
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Domains and Dataset collection details</h2>

<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multiple Optimal Actions and Expert Policies</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During the collection of our dataset, we need an expert policy.
However, in many domains, there might exist multiple optimal actions at the same time.
In Cliff Walking, the expert policy is hand-coded and we enumerated all optimal actions for all states.
In MiniGrid Door key and MiniGrid Four Rooms, we use exhaustive search to enumerate all possible optimal actions.
In ALFWorld and HeirachyCraft, a built-in planner can serve as an expert policy.
Although these planners give an optimal action for each state, they do not yield the full set of all optimal actions.
Consequently, we cannot use these planners to compute the ground truth feedback for cases where there are multiple optimal actions.
For these two domains, we also use exhaustive search to enumerate all possible actions, and consider action optimal if after taking this action, there exists some sequence of remaining actions that reaches the goal in the same number of steps as the planner.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Preference and Binary Feedback</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the sampling policies only to sample states.
When constructing our preference and preference dataset for discrete domains, given a state, we enumerate all legal actions (for binary feedback) and all combinations of legal actions (for preference).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Robomimic</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Robomimic, the continuous action space of the domain means we cannot enumerate all optimal actions.
In Robomimic experiments, we use an imitation learning policy as an expert policy, which gives 100% success rate in the task.
We also conducted an empirical study to decide the threshold distance for optimal actions. We injected different scales of random noise into the actions and inspect the task success rate and found 0.28 is the threshold of noise where bigger noise starts to negatively impact the success rate.
Therefore, we use this threshold as the biggest possible distance from the imitation learning policy action for an action to be optimal.
We also use this threshold for delta actions.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Feedback Model Error Examples</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present some wrong responses from LLM.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A7.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="179.77" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 179.77" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,179.77) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 173.86 C 0 177.12 2.64 179.77 5.91 179.77 L 544.09 179.77 C 547.36 179.77 550 177.12 550 173.86 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 155.66 L 548.03 155.66 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 164.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A7.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Wrong response example in Cliff Walking Binary Feedback</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:34.88em;--ltx-fo-height:9.15em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="130.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 126.61)" width="482.64"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:34.88em;">
<span id="A7.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are in position (0, 4). Is action DOWN the best action you can take?</span></span><pre id="A7.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
{ "reasoning": "The agent’s goal is to reach (3, 11) from (0, 4).
Action DOWN moves to (1, 4).
While this starts descending, reaching row 3 safely requires avoiding holes
in columns 1-10. Moving right from (0, 4) toward column 11 first ensures a
direct path to the goal without risking holes. Moving down now doesn’t shorten
the path and delays aligning with the safe column (11). Thus, moving right
is better than down.",
"feedback": "NO"
}

</pre>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A7.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In the example above, the LM assumes that they also need to keep away from the cliff, as well as give a wrong expectation of steps to the goal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A7.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="129.96" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 129.96" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,129.96) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 124.05 C 0 127.31 2.64 129.96 5.91 129.96 L 544.09 129.96 C 547.36 129.96 550 127.31 550 124.05 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 105.85 L 548.03 105.85 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 114.44)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A7.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Wrong response example in HiearchyCraft Action Advising</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:5.55em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" class="ltx_minipage" height="80.26" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 76.8)" width="34.88em"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><pre id="A7.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;Prompt Omitted&gt;
{"reasoning": "I need to find a way to get diamond, and I need to craft a furnace
to smelt the ore. I have wood plank and stick, so I can craft a furnace. I also
need to find iron ore or gold ore to smelt. I can search for wood at the swamp to
get more wood and craft more items.",
"action": "search for wood at swamp"}’
</pre></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A7.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In the example above, the LM does not have knowledge of system dynamics. Even if it correctly reasons that it needs to collect more wood, it still picks the non-optimal action.
This action is not optimal because, moving to the forest and subsequently searching for wood leads to a shorter path to the goal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A7.p6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="817.96" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 817.96" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,817.96) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 812.06 C 0 815.32 2.64 817.96 5.91 817.96 L 544.09 817.96 C 547.36 817.96 550 815.32 550 812.06 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 793.85 L 548.03 793.85 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 802.45)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A7.p6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Wrong response example in Door Key Preference</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:34.88em;--ltx-fo-height:55.27em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="768.27" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 764.81)" width="482.64"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:34.88em;">
<span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You need to solve Minigrid Doorkey.
<br class="ltx_break">Minigrid Doorkey involves crossing a gridworld, where you need to pick up the key, unlock the door and reach the goal. Do not hit the wall.
<br class="ltx_break">The state is described with an ASCII art. In the ASCII art, “#” means wall. “K” means key. “D” means door. “G” means goal. “.” means empty tile. “ˆ” means the agent who is facing upwards. “V” means the agent who is facing downwards. “&lt;” means the agent who is facing leftwards. “&gt;” means the agent who is facing rightwards.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The possible actions are:</span></span>
<span id="A7.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">TURN LEFT, changing the direction to left, for example, the agent “ˆ” will become “&lt;”.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">TURN RIGHT, changing the direction to right, for example, the agent “ˆ” will become “&gt;”.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">MOVE FORWARD, moving forwards for one tile</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A7.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<span id="A7.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A7.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">PICK UP THE KEY, picking up the key, this is only possible when you are facing the tile with key on it</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A7.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<span id="A7.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A7.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">UNLOCK THE DOOR, this action is only possible when you have the key.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You will be asked to compare two actions given a state and provide preference.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are in the following state represented in ASCII art:</span></span><pre id="A7.p6.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
#####
#.#.#
#&gt;D.#
#.#G#
#####
</pre>
<span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The door is unlocked. You have the key.
<br class="ltx_break">Given <span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MOVE FORWARD</span> or <span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TURN LEFT</span>, which action is better? Please think step by step.
<br class="ltx_break">Only give the answer in a new line in JSON format:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{"reasoning": &lt;REASONING&gt;, "preference": &lt;PREFERENCE&gt;}
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Where <span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PREFERENCE&gt;</span> is one of “FIRST” or “SECOND”, <span id="A7.p6.pic1.2.6.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;REASONING&gt;</span> is a string of your thinking steps.</span></span><pre id="A7.p6.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{
  "reasoning": "In the current state, the agent is facing downwards and the door
  is unlocked. Moving forward is not a good option as it will lead to hitting the
  wall. Turning left is a better option as it allows the agent to change
  direction without moving and potentially see new possibilities to
  reach the goal.",
  "preference": "SECOND"
}
</pre>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A7.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p7.1" class="ltx_p">In the wrong response example above, the LM misinterprets the observation and deems itself facing downwards, which leads to a wrong response in preferring the non-optimal action <span id="A7.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TURN LEFT</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="A7.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A7.p8.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="335.26" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 335.26" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,335.26) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF0000;" fill="#BF0000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 329.36 C 0 332.62 2.64 335.26 5.91 335.26 L 544.09 335.26 C 547.36 335.26 550 332.62 550 329.36 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 311.15 L 548.03 311.15 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 319.75)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.p8.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A7.p8.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p8.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Wrong response example in Door Key Image Observation Action Advising</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:20.39em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="285.56" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 282.1)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.p8.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A7.p8.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p8.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;Prompt Omitted&gt;</span></span>
<span id="A7.p8.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p8.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is your image observation.</span></span><img src="2509.09790v1/pics/doorkey/obs2.png" id="A7.p8.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:202/202;" width="202" height="202" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"><pre id="A7.p8.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{"reasoning": "I am currently facing right and need to move towards the
goal which is directly ahead. Since there’s no obstacle in my path, I
can move forward.", "action": "MOVE FORWARD"}
</pre>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A7.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p9.1" class="ltx_p">In this wrong response example, the VLM misrecognises the position of the goal and disregards the wall ahead and decides to move forward, which will lead the agent to hit the wall.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Reproducibility Statement</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The experiment details are converted throughout the paper as well as the appendix. For reproducibility, we included details in the dataset collection and evaluation pipelines in Section <a href="#S2" title="2 Methodology ‣ How well can LLMs provide planning feedback in grounded environments?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. We provide the prompt examples in Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Verbalisation and Prompt Examples ‣ How well can LLMs provide planning feedback in grounded environments?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> and more implementation details in Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Domains and Dataset collection details ‣ How well can LLMs provide planning feedback in grounded environments?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>.
We use models that are open-source and publicly available and we also provide a code and dataset appendix. We will also open-source our codebase.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
